      "location": "page summary, second paragraph",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The page says the closed surfaces v_{i,j} 'have triangular unit pairings with the dual classes x_{i,j}'. The opened integral-module theorem, proof 1.1, explicitly says the actual absolute-cycle pairing matrix multiplies each relative row by a nonzero closing factor and that 'These factors are not asserted to be Laurent units'. Already at n=2 the diagonal pairing is a Laurent unit times (1-q)²(1+qt)(1-t), which is not a unit: its augmentation q=t=1 is zero. Unit diagonal pairings belong to the relative classes v'_{i,j}.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "66d0423a2a9530a5bf665c400e97c43623dc09ea861fee86e0d70dec0e3a4d21"
