      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "[F1] places the square and triangle classes in H2(C-tilde,nu-tilde) and then says 'the endpoints may lie in P or on ∂D'. Boundary endpoints require a boundary-relative group. Two disjoint boundary-to-boundary chords, as used in this item's [F2], give a square whose outer boundary lies in ∂C-tilde and need not lie in nu-tilde; it therefore is not the asserted end-relative cycle. The opened def-relative-singular-homology requires the representative's boundary to lie in the relative subspace. [Bigelow 2002, section 3.1](https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0204057) distinguishes puncture-ended squares, boundary-ended squares, and mixed-endpoint squares by their respective relative groups.",
